# Accepted differences between the SDL server and the X11 reference,
# per test: the maximum number of differing image pixels (-1: any), and
# whether standard output may differ. Anything not listed must match
# exactly. The SDL server draws with gcon's own rasterizer (as the
# headless server does: graphics/raster), by X's rules but with arcs
# flattened to polygons, where X rasterizes them exactly (with room over
# 2, 3 and 13 when recorded); its text is the platform's fonts.
#
# name      pixels  output
clipcopy    6       same     # arc edges
lines       6       same     # arc edges
shapes      20      same     # the edges of a filled circle and a pie
text        -1      differs  # different fonts: glyphs and metrics
